            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite technologic advances in many diagnostic fields, the 12-lead ECG remains the basis for early identification and management of an acute coronary syndrome. This article reviews the use of the ECG in acute coronary syndromes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
